          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called the
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              \-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              system
            is a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            defined on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            are pairs consisting of a
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            demand these fields to be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+differential+forms"} holomorphic differential forms
          %p The name results from the traditional symbols for these fields, which are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\gamma,\beta) \in \Omega^{0,\bullet}(X) \oplus \Omega^{1, \bullet}(X)
                  \\,.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We state the definition of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            = succeed "-system" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
            (see there) in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gwilliam"} Gwilliam, section 6.1
          %p We first give the standard variant of the theory, the
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AbelianMasslessTheory"}> Abelian massless theory
              \.
          %p Then we consider the
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AbelianMassiveTheory"} Abelian massive theory
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#HolomorphicChernSimonsTheory"} Holomorphic Chern-Simons theory
          %h3#AbelianMasslessTheory Abelian massless theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
          %p
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinematics"} kinematics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      E \coloneqq \wedge^{0,\bullet}\Gamma(T X) \oplus \wedge^{1,\bullet} \Gamma(T X)
            %li
              %p
                hence the (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"}> abelian
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+sections"} local sections
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathcal{E} = \Omega_X^{0,\bullet} \oplus \Omega_X^{1, \bullet}
                      \\,,
              %p we write
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi c
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_c \hookrightarrow \Gamma_X(E)
              %p
                for the sections of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compact support
            %li
              %p the local pairing
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mi loc
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Dens
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\langle -,-\rangle_{loc} \colon E \otimes E \to Dens_X
              %p
                with values in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+bundle"} density bundle
                is given by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+product"} wedge product
                followed by projection on the
                = succeed "-forms" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mi loc
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\langle \gamma_1 + \beta_1, \gamma_2, \beta_2\rangle_{loc}
                      \\coloneqq
                      (\gamma_1 \wedge \beta_2 + \gamma_2 \wedge \beta_1)_{|(1,1)}
            %li
              %p hence the global pairing
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi c
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\langle -,-\rangle \colon \mathcal{E}_c \otimes \mathcal{E}_c \to \mathbb{C}
              %p is given by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mi loc
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi γ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mn 1
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\langle \gamma_1 + \beta_1, \gamma_2, \beta_2\rangle_{loc}
                      \\coloneqq
                      \\int_{X}\left(\gamma_1 \wedge \beta_2 + \gamma_2 \wedge \beta_1\right)
          %p
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Q \colon \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}
              %p
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+differential"} Dolbeault differential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \partial
            %li
              %p
                hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+complex"} elliptic complex
                of fields is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\mathcal{E}, Q) = (\Omega_X^{0,\bullet}\oplus \Omega_X^{1,\bullet}, \bar \partial)
              %p
                is the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+complex"} Dolbeault complex
            %li
              %p
                and hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      S \colon \mathcal{E}_c \to \mathcal{C}
              %p is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi γ
                              %mo +
                              %mi β
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mn 2
                              %msub
                                %mo ∫
                                %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                              %mi γ
                              %mo +
                              %mi β
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mover
                                %mo ∂
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi γ
                              %mo +
                              %mi β
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mo ∫
                                %mi X
                              %mi β
                              %mo ∧
                              %mover
                                %mo ∂
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                              %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      (\gamma + \beta) &amp; \mapsto
                      \\frac{1}{2}\int_X \langle \gamma+ \beta, \; \bar \partial (\gamma + \beta)\rangle
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =  \int_X \beta \wedge \bar \partial \gamma
                      \\end{aligned}
          %h3#AbelianMassiveTheory Abelian massive theory
          %p (…)
          %h3#HolomorphicChernSimonsTheory Holomorphic Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            …
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+Chern-Simons+theory"}> holomorphic Chern-Simons theory
            …
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#eulerlagrange_equations_of_motion Euler-Lagrange equations of motion
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi γ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi β
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\bar \partial \gamma = 0
                  \\;\;,
                  \\;\;
                  \\bar \partial\beta = 0
                  \\,.
          %h2#relation_with_models
            Relation with
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{1,1}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1,1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi q
                  %mo ∧
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S[q,\gamma] = \int_X \partial q \wedge \bar{\partial}\gamma,
          %p
            which has an abelian right-moving Kac-Moody symmetry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\mapsto q+\lambda
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\lambda=0
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetry"} gauge symmetry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} gauged
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi β
                  %mi q
                  %mo ∧
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{\mathrm{gauged}}[q,\gamma] = \int_X \partial_\beta q \wedge \bar{\partial}\gamma,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi β
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_\beta q := \partial q + \beta
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\in\Omega^{1,\bullet}(X)
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection"} connection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q=0
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            system with action
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi β
                  %mo ,
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∧
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mi γ
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{\beta\gamma}[\beta,\gamma] = \int_X \beta \wedge \bar{\partial}\gamma.
          %p
            Thus, a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            system can be interpreted as a chiral (or Kac-Moody) quotient along a null killing vector of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            with target space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1,1}
            (
            %a{:href => "#LinRoc20"}> LinRoc20
            ).
