          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-quantization"} BV-quantization
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras"} factorization algebras
            is in chapter 6 of
          %ul#Gwilliam
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"}> Owen Gwilliam
              ,
              %em Factorization algebras and free field theories
              PhD thesis (
              %a{:href => "https://people.math.umass.edu/~gwilliam/thesis.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A construction of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+differential+operator"} chiral differential operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\gamma
            system in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV+formalism"} BV formalism
            with an intermediate step using factorization algebras:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassily+Gorbounov"}> Vassily Gorbounov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral differential operators via Batalin-Vilkovisky quantization
                %a{:href => "http://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/gwilliam/cdo.pdf"} pdf
            %li#LinRoc20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Lindstrom"}> Ulf Lindstrom
                ,
                = succeed "," do
